{title: Evening rehearsal}
{artist: Music Catalog studies}
{key: C}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}
{comment: Easy, with a steady pulse}

{start_of_verse: Intro}
[C]One, two, [Am]find the time
[F]Let each [G]note unwind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Leave a little [G]room to breathe
[Am]Hear the spaces [F]in between
[C]Every part has [G]its own place
[F]Every voice a [G]little space
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Keep the rhythm [C]running slow
[Am]Let the melody [G]find its own
[F]Side by side and [C]beat by beat
[Dm]Bring it back to [G]one with [C]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Listen for the [G]softer sound
[Am]Let the bass line [F]hold the ground
[C]When the harmony [G]comes around
[F]Leave the final [G]measure out
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dm]Take a breath and [Am]start again
[F]Count the bars from [G]one to ten
[Dm]Every change a [Am]place to meet
[F]Find the song beneath our [G]feet
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Final chorus}
[F]Keep the rhythm [C]running slow
[Am]Let the melody [G]find its own
[F]Side by side and [C]beat by beat
[Dm]Bring it back to [G]one with [C]me
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]Let the last note [G]ring
[C]Let the last note ring
{end_of_verse}
